WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.692
- I am very excited that
you use your platform

00:00:01.692 --> 00:00:03.010
to shine a light on things

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.090
that maybe not everybody knows about.

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:04.923
This is really cool.

00:00:04.923 --> 00:00:05.756
- Well, that's how I
feel about you, as well.

00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:07.330
Yes, my manager, who I've been with

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:09.040
since I was literally 14 years old,

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.350
been with my entire team since I was

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.832
basically 14, 15 years old--

00:00:11.832 --> 00:00:13.240
- [Kelly] Wow!
- So we've become very close.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.689
Her son has a very rare disorder,
disease, called EB, EBMRF,

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:20.790
and it's very rare, and
nobody really knows about it.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.240
And we're trying to get the
word out about it, spread some--

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.073
- I had never heard about it!

00:00:23.073 --> 00:00:24.290
- Most people haven't,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.440
and then you see it and you hear about it,

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.010
and it's really tough,

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.300
and he lives with this every single day.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.587
And this family is amazing,

00:00:29.587 --> 00:00:32.980
and we just wanna find a
cure for this effing thing,

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.020
sooner than later.
- [Kelly] Yes, yes! (claps)

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.450
- See, the f-word again! (laughs)

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:36.662
(crowd cheers)

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:37.837
- My next guess is a family

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.975
that's close personal friends with Kaley

00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:41.617
and is coping with a rare illness

00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:44.470
that is as tragic as it is mysterious.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.430
Take a look.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:46.563
- Ooh, hi, kitty!

00:00:46.563 --> 00:00:47.890
- I'm Brandon.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:51.050
I am 15 years old, and I live
in Los Angeles, California.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.614
I have epidermolysis bullosa,

00:00:52.614 --> 00:00:56.030
which is a skin condition
that you're born with,

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.990
which means I have very fragile skin.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:02.040
- Basically, you're missing the
gene that produces collagen,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.590
which binds the layers
of the skin together.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:08.060
- Brandon wants to participate
as fully as he can,

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.030
and when he has bad days
and can't get out of bed,

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.510
it's just, it's really,
it's heartbreaking.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.877
- And he deals with an enormous challenge

00:01:15.877 --> 00:01:18.237
quite gracefully, I think.

00:01:18.237 --> 00:01:20.580
- I want people to know that, yeah,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.650
it doesn't define me,

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.760
and there's gonna be
good days and bad days,

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.200
And I try to just get over the bad days

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.110
and just keep hoping for the good days.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.400
- [Andrea] We are amazed everyday

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.400
at his ability to just wake
up and deal as best he can,

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.656
and life is tough, but so is he.

00:01:38.656 --> 00:01:40.293
(claps)

00:01:40.293 --> 00:01:41.665
- Y'all, please welcome
(crowd cheers)

00:01:41.665 --> 00:01:44.273
Andrea Pett-Joseph, her
husband Paul Joseph,

00:01:44.273 --> 00:01:45.640
and their son Brandon.

